From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 05:50:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: g16: Check the session once per pass by
 default

Measured with g16_check_once 0 against 1 on experimental 1.1087, five
interleaved blocks: compute.light depth 1 179.2 -> 150.6 us (-16.0 %),
depth 8 39.6 -> 32.9 us (-16.8 %), depth 64 19.0 -> 19.0 us;
render.light depth 1 185.2 -> 170.3 us (-8.1 %), depths 8 and 64 within
1.1 %; compute.heavy and render.heavy within 0.3 %; stress clean and no
GPU fault.

Turn g16_check_once on by default. Within one pass under the device
lock, the transport check at the head of check_hangs then reuses the
session check that the same pass already ran and passed, instead of
running Session::check again. A pass that opens no scope, and recover(),
which loops transport_error() for up to a second, still run the full
check every time. Writing 0 at run time restores the old behaviour.

No memory and no new state: one static verdict word written only under
the device lock and two counters.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/params.rs | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/params.rs b/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/params.rs
index b1ac6a7cf2..19af0b831b 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/params.rs
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/params.rs
@@ -2364,8 +2364,8 @@ pub(crate) fn submit_retire() -> bool {
     "G16: 1 = a submission first retires the commands that completed since the last poll pass, without waiting for the firmware's event, then publishes (default 0: off; runtime 0644)"
 );
 
-/// Storage of `g16_check_once` (runtime 0644, default 0).
-static CHECK_ONCE: AtomicU32 = AtomicU32::new(0);
+/// Storage of `g16_check_once` (runtime 0644, default 1).
+static CHECK_ONCE: AtomicU32 = AtomicU32::new(1);
 
 /// `g16_check_once` = 1: the transport check at the head of check_hangs reuses the session
 /// check its own pass already ran and passed ([`super::check_once`]). 0: it runs the session
@@ -2380,7 +2380,7 @@ pub(crate) fn check_once() -> u32 {
     CHECK_ONCE_PARM,
     CHECK_ONCE,
     "g16_check_once",
-    "G16: 1 = within one pass, check_hangs reuses the session check that pass already ran and passed (default 0: it checks again; runtime 0644)"
+    "G16: 1 = within one pass, check_hangs reuses the session check that pass already ran and passed (default 1; 0 = it checks again; runtime 0644)"
 );
 
 /// Storage of `g16_submit_defer` (runtime 0644, default 16).
